---
import Refugios from "../../../layouts/Refugios.astro";

/**
 * The single failure page for everything that can go wrong with a code.
 *
 * A wrong code, an expired one, one whose five attempts are gone, one superseded by a newer
 * request, a token that names nothing, and a token minted for an address that belongs to
 * nobody all land here with the same words. **The collapsing is the security property**, not
 * a shortcut: a page that said "expired" rather than "wrong" would confirm that a code had
 * been issued, which confirms the address is registered — the oracle ADR 0008 forbids.
 *
 * It is also, usefully, the complete answer. The shelter's next move is to ask for another
 * code in every one of those cases, so a more specific message would not change what anyone
 * does about it.
 */
---

<Refugios title="Ese código no sirvió" heading="Ese código no sirvió">
  <p data-testid="code-refused">
    Puede que lo hayas escrito distinto, que se haya vencido, o que hayas pedido otro después
    — al pedir uno nuevo, el anterior deja de servir.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/refugios/entrar/codigo">Vuelve a escribirlo</a> si crees que fue un dedazo, o
    <a href="/refugios/entrar">pide un código nuevo</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <!--
      Said plainly because the alternative is a shelter concluding it has been locked out of
      its own account. Five wrong guesses kill the *code*, and nothing else: no shelter, no
      session, no waiting period. The next request works.
    -->
    Después de varios intentos fallidos el código se anula por seguridad. Eso no bloquea tu
    refugio: pides otro y sigues.
  </p>
</Refugios>
